# walk.play — a session, not a unit. Every row goes through flow_move/flow_action,
# the same intents the host applies and an observer replays.
#
# The claims here are RELATIONS wherever a relation is the real claim, so a content
# or tuning change does not turn this red for no reason. Where an exact number IS
# the claim, the comment above it says why.

genesis 1337 1
echo --- a fresh warrior, before anything has happened

# The kit is granted at genesis (flow_genesis runs bundle_activate) — a replica that
# skipped that boot step was a real bug, which is why genesis is shared at all.
expect inv > 0
expect alive == 1
expect hp > 0
expect depth == 1

# ⚠ HP AT FULL IS THE CLAIM, NOT A NUMBER. Whatever the class tuning says the pool is,
# an untouched warrior starts at it; `hp == hpmax` survives every retune of the pool.
expect hp == hpmax

echo --- turning is FREE: the distance clock must not advance on a pure turn
# The clock is distance-driven (every HEX_LEN travelled = one sim_tick), so a spin
# costs nothing. If turning ever starts ticking, the whole cost model has moved and
# this row is the cheapest place to notice.
note msgs
move 0 1 24
expect alive == 1
expect hp == hpmax

echo --- glide forward across several hexes
move 1 0 120
expect alive == 1

# Gliding cannot leave the level by itself: a depth change needs a stair walked onto.
expect depth == 1

echo --- wait in place: the one intent that forces the clock without moving
wait 10
expect alive == 1

echo --- try to pick up whatever is underfoot (harmless when nothing is)
act 2 0 0
expect inv > 0

echo --- the world survived the whole session
expect alive == 1
expect hp <= hpmax
expect gold >= 0
